Design a circuit that performs a multiplication operation on a 32-bit input by a fixed scalar (specifically, multiplying by 1664). The module takes a 32-bit input and leverages bit shifts and additions to calculate the product, outputting a 32-bit result. The implementation efficiently utilizes combinational logic to execute the series of operations necessary for the multiplication, ensuring the output reflects the multiplication of the input by the defined factor.
