description:
Design a synchronous memory module with 64KB (2^14) of addressable space, supporting read and write operations. The memory is accessed based on an 18-bit address input, where the upper 4 bits are used to enable memory access only for addresses within a specific range (0 to 15), preventing access to the remaining memory beyond this region. On a positive clock edge, if the reset is inactive and a write signal is asserted along with an appropriate address, data is stored in the memory. When the read signal is active, the module outputs the data stored at the specified address, while also providing a wait request signal, which in this design is always deasserted.
module top_module(

	i_clk, i_reset_n,
	i_address, i_write, i_read, i_writedata,

	o_readdata, o_waitrequest
);

