Implement a 4-bit to 2-bit converter that maps specific input values to predetermined 2-bit output codes based on defined ranges. For inputs ranging from 0 to 4, the output is 00; for inputs 5 to 8, the output is 01; for inputs 9 to 11, the output is 10; and for any input value greater than 11, the output defaults to 11. This design serves to categorize input values into a limited set of output states.
